## caveats
1. cpu_model:unknown is expected here, not a failure: this vendor kernel's /proc/cpuinfo carries
   no "model name" and no "Hardware" line (only processor/Features/Serial), so crypto.c's probe
   finds nothing. The board is RK3588 (8x Cortex-A76/A55, 3 frequency policies, 2.304 GHz on cpu4).
2. cpu_mhz:1800 in the RESULT header is cpu0's scaling_cur_freq (A55 cluster, 1.8 GHz), because
   crypto.c reads cpu0 unconditionally. The measured thread ran on cpu4 at 2304 MHz, so the
   cycles_per_byte column is scaled with 1800 MHz and understates true cpu4 cycles by 2304/1800 = 1.28x.
   Use ns_per_byte (clock-independent) for cross-host comparison; true cpu4 cycles/byte =
   ns_per_byte x 2.304 (e.g. chacha20x4 -> 3.54 c/B, chacha8x4 -> 1.60 c/B).
3. cpu_flags line only prints the probe's shortlist (asimd aes pmull); the full /proc/cpuinfo Features
   set is recorded in section 1 and also includes sha1/sha2/crc32/atomics/asimddp/asimdrdm/lrcpc/dcpop.
4. No SVE/SVE2 on this SoC, so the x4 path is plain NEON 4-lane (QR4V), as intended.
5. No failures: all 3 invocations completed, all 18 RESULT lines emitted, exit status 0.
